WEBVTT

01:39.974 --> 01:42.185
You've got one of those little
smoke signals, right?

01:44.229 --> 01:46.606
It lets you talk to people far away.

01:46.689 --> 01:48.358
You were using it earlier.

01:48.858 --> 01:50.693
Oh, my smartphone?

01:51.569 --> 01:53.571
Tell Asa to come here.

01:54.906 --> 01:56.533
I want to talk to her.

02:00.286 --> 02:02.163
You want to talk?

02:02.247 --> 02:04.707
Not gonna tell us to hand her over?

02:05.500 --> 02:09.504
Higashi Village doesn't want both twins?

02:09.587 --> 02:11.422
That's not my concern.

02:11.506 --> 02:12.966
I came here on my own today.

02:13.883 --> 02:17.345
Then you should come
to the Kagemori manor.

02:17.428 --> 02:20.431
Asa-san has been wanting to see you, too.

02:20.515 --> 02:23.560
Who walks into a bear's den?

02:23.643 --> 02:24.853
Tell her to come here.

02:24.936 --> 02:28.356
Do you think you have a choice?

02:28.857 --> 02:30.066
Wait, wait.

02:30.567 --> 02:33.236
Could you at least let us
stop Jin-san's bleeding?

02:33.903 --> 02:34.737
He'll die.

02:35.738 --> 02:39.450
I made sure not to kill him,
but very well.

02:39.534 --> 02:41.619
You cut shallow on purpose?

02:41.703 --> 02:45.123
Because you, uh... Jin, right?

02:45.206 --> 02:46.583
I could tell you weren't
trying to kill me.

02:47.959 --> 02:52.005
If you were, I wouldn't
have held back either.

02:52.589 --> 02:56.467
Mountain folk cut off
from modern civilization are scary.

02:57.760 --> 03:02.640
If he'd meant to kill me
with his first attack, I'd be dead.

03:08.855 --> 03:11.649
The fish belong to four-eyes.

03:11.733 --> 03:15.278
And the hare and tortoise are his.

03:15.361 --> 03:18.281
There's another pair somewhere.

03:18.364 --> 03:19.908
Are they yours?

03:19.991 --> 03:23.036
Yeah, they're mine. They're around.

03:23.786 --> 03:25.580
Why didn't you use them?

03:26.080 --> 03:28.291
Are they not suited to battle?

03:28.374 --> 03:29.459
Oh, no.

03:29.542 --> 03:31.044
They've been here the whole time.

03:35.715 --> 03:38.176
They're just too big to fit in here.

03:39.344 --> 03:41.596
If you want, I could make them try.

03:42.680 --> 03:45.391
I'm not bringing Asa-san here.

03:45.475 --> 03:48.394
If you'll come to the Kagemori manor,

03:48.478 --> 03:51.397
no harm will come to you.

03:52.899 --> 03:56.444
You understand that
I don't want to kill you, right?

03:59.989 --> 04:02.700
The hare and tortoise, plus that.

04:03.368 --> 04:05.578
That would be tough for Right and Left.

04:09.249 --> 04:11.960
Fine. I'll go.

04:13.002 --> 04:15.713
So don't be rude
to Right and Left anymore.

04:17.423 --> 04:18.883
That goes without saying.

04:19.467 --> 04:22.136
You'll be treated as guests.

04:22.720 --> 04:25.974
Now that that's settled, take us to Asa.

04:26.057 --> 04:26.891
Actually...

04:27.558 --> 04:29.978
We need to clean this up first.

04:31.062 --> 04:33.898
Ai-chan, another job for you.

04:37.694 --> 04:41.531
Scavenger always makes a terrible mess.

04:41.614 --> 04:43.116
Sca... what?

04:43.866 --> 04:46.661
Scavenger. Nature's janitors.

04:46.744 --> 04:48.871
Ai-chan eats everything.

04:49.580 --> 04:51.833
Makoto-kun produces those things at will.

04:54.627 --> 04:57.505
I regularly feed them
all sorts of useful things

04:57.588 --> 04:59.424
so I can be ready for anything.

04:59.924 --> 05:02.218
Since they're janitors,

05:02.302 --> 05:05.430
I sometimes feed them things
the world's better without.

05:05.513 --> 05:06.347
They're quite convenient.

05:07.056 --> 05:10.268
For raids, hijackings, and terror attacks,

05:10.351 --> 05:13.438
with Makoto-kun,
I don't get caught by security.

05:14.105 --> 05:16.649
That was a lot of words I don't know,

05:16.733 --> 05:18.443
but I get that they're convenient.

05:19.694 --> 05:20.945
Your Daemons.

05:21.612 --> 05:25.325
- Yes?
- How many kan is that tortoise?

05:25.408 --> 05:29.829
Kan? Oh, how many kilograms is that?

05:29.912 --> 05:32.498
I don't know. I've never weighed them,

05:32.582 --> 05:34.834
but they can get even heavier.

05:41.424 --> 05:44.594
I require more training.

05:46.220 --> 05:47.847
So disciplined!

05:56.355 --> 05:59.650
Yuru, are you good at hunting rabbits?

05:59.734 --> 06:02.153
What? You use traps for rabbits.

06:03.029 --> 06:04.739
They make a good broth.

06:04.822 --> 06:06.407
Barbarian!

06:06.908 --> 06:09.243
Can Daemons even be eaten?

06:10.203 --> 06:11.746
Is someone there?

06:11.829 --> 06:14.373
Oh, hello. Security?

06:14.874 --> 06:16.834
All the lights suddenly went out.

06:16.918 --> 06:17.794
It's quite inconvenient.

06:20.088 --> 06:21.005
What is this?

06:21.672 --> 06:23.925
All the lights are broken.

06:24.008 --> 06:25.635
Maybe they short-circuited.

06:25.718 --> 06:28.429
They scared us when they
suddenly started crackling.

06:28.513 --> 06:29.597
I see...

06:30.890 --> 06:33.267
The lights are on in this stairwell.

06:33.351 --> 06:35.019
You can exit through here.

06:35.686 --> 06:38.523
Okay. Thank you.

06:54.455 --> 06:56.624
Gabby-chan! Gabby-chan! Gabby-chan!

06:57.416 --> 06:59.252
- What? Are we under attack?!
- You won't believe this.

06:59.335 --> 07:01.546
Jin-san's bringing my brother here.

07:01.629 --> 07:04.006
Seriously? He's fast.

07:04.090 --> 07:06.300
What am I going to do? What should I wear?

07:07.301 --> 07:10.221
I dunno. When'd you get so girly?

07:14.225 --> 07:17.145
It's Jin. Sorry to bother you so late.

07:18.146 --> 07:20.189
I've settled matters
with the Higashi Village twin.

07:20.690 --> 07:23.568
Yes, with Yuru-kun.

07:23.651 --> 07:25.528
We're on our way to the manor.

07:25.611 --> 07:27.155
What a long cave.

07:27.238 --> 07:30.116
Really? Well done.

07:30.616 --> 07:33.494
Could you have him wait until I get back?

07:33.578 --> 07:36.247
Where are you, Master?

07:36.998 --> 07:38.082
At a hot spring.

07:39.625 --> 07:45.131
I thought I'd take an after-work bath,
but I'll head straight back.

07:45.756 --> 07:47.508
Don't be rude to Yuru-kun.

08:16.496 --> 08:17.538
We're here.

08:18.122 --> 08:19.290
This is the Kagemori clan home.

08:39.018 --> 08:42.980
We heard the Kagemoris had
several Daemon Wielders...

08:44.023 --> 08:46.067
but I don't sense a thing.

08:46.150 --> 08:47.652
There are plenty around.

08:48.319 --> 08:51.197
We're just not in the VIP area yet.

08:51.280 --> 08:52.490
VIP?

08:52.573 --> 08:53.658
Limited access.

08:54.492 --> 08:56.160
The edge of the barrier's up there.

09:16.639 --> 09:17.765
Whoa!

09:17.848 --> 09:18.766
Unbelievable.

09:19.392 --> 09:21.269
They're everywhere.

09:21.352 --> 09:24.355
There are so many, I can't tell
how many pairs there are.

09:28.609 --> 09:30.486
Asa, your brother's here.

09:30.570 --> 09:31.654
He's here?

09:31.737 --> 09:33.823
Do you want to go with me?

09:33.906 --> 09:37.660
No, I don't want to see the guy
who put two holes in my body.

09:37.743 --> 09:39.662
It still hurts to walk.

09:41.622 --> 09:42.665
I'll be back.

09:43.249 --> 09:44.333
Good luck.

09:45.293 --> 09:47.336
I'm gonna sleep.

09:58.681 --> 10:00.308
A big building?

10:00.391 --> 10:01.976
That's one big plot.

10:04.854 --> 10:05.605
KAGEMORI PARK, KAGEMORI VISION

10:05.688 --> 10:06.439
KAGEMORI, KAGEMORI GOLF CLUB, KAGEMORI ZOO

10:11.485 --> 10:13.821
You think he got caught?

10:13.904 --> 10:17.408
I hate to think that could happen
with Right and Left accompanying him.

10:18.367 --> 10:22.413
Oh, well. Daddy's off to pick up his son.

10:22.997 --> 10:24.749
Want me to drive?

10:24.832 --> 10:29.962
No. They don't know we're associated yet.

10:30.463 --> 10:32.173
I'll take a cab.

10:32.840 --> 10:33.674
How will you get back?

10:34.342 --> 10:35.718
By train.

10:36.218 --> 10:38.929
It'll be a social studies lesson.

10:47.772 --> 10:49.732
The entrance is huge!

10:49.815 --> 10:51.692
Like a castle on the plains.

10:52.526 --> 10:54.195
It's rather late.

10:55.237 --> 10:56.947
You're such a dedicated worker, Jin.

10:57.031 --> 10:59.241
Hey, Asuma-san.

11:00.034 --> 11:01.994
What are you doing here?

11:02.578 --> 11:06.082
I heard the other twin was coming,
so I came to entertain him.

11:08.334 --> 11:10.336
I don't believe I told you about that.

11:11.837 --> 11:14.840
I've got really good hearing. Oh?

11:14.924 --> 11:16.342
You're hurt?

11:16.967 --> 11:18.511
It's not serious.

11:19.512 --> 11:21.764
Did you get into a fight with them?

11:22.390 --> 11:24.892
What magnificent Daemons.

11:25.643 --> 11:28.145
And are you Asa-san's brother?

11:31.357 --> 11:33.984
I'm Kagemori Asuma. Nice to meet you.

11:34.568 --> 11:36.237
B-Brother!

11:42.326 --> 11:44.245
Brother...

11:44.954 --> 11:46.789
You're not dead?! You're alive?!

11:46.872 --> 11:48.249
What kind of greeting is that?

11:48.332 --> 11:50.876
- Can I hug you?!
- No!

11:51.710 --> 11:54.380
Sorry. I don't know
how close we are anymore.

11:54.463 --> 11:55.714
Neither do I.

11:57.508 --> 11:59.468
I didn't come to make friends.

11:59.552 --> 12:01.595
I came because I have questions for you.

12:01.679 --> 12:03.764
Sure. Ask me anything.

12:03.848 --> 12:05.766
Once we're done talking, can I hug you?

12:05.850 --> 12:07.017
I said no!

12:07.560 --> 12:09.770
You're so badass when you're being cold.

12:10.521 --> 12:13.941
Instead of obsessing over me,
you should be worried about his injury.

12:14.817 --> 12:16.527
Jin-san, you need to get to the infirmary!

12:16.610 --> 12:21.407
Given Jin's condition, why don't
I show you around the manor?

12:21.991 --> 12:24.285
Huh? You're here, Asuma-san?

12:24.368 --> 12:27.163
Wow, you're blind to everything
except your brother.

12:27.788 --> 12:31.208
Yuru-kun is our guest.

12:31.292 --> 12:32.835
We have no business with you.

12:33.419 --> 12:34.420
Okay, okay.

12:35.379 --> 12:37.756
Make yourself at home, Yuru-kun.

12:44.013 --> 12:46.932
Akio, stay outside the barrier.

12:47.016 --> 12:48.392
Don't let anyone in.

12:48.976 --> 12:49.810
Yes, sir.

12:50.478 --> 12:54.190
Mr. Big Brother, stay close to me
while you're inside the manor.

12:54.857 --> 12:56.484
You'll get lost.

13:02.239 --> 13:05.284
Oh, you're going to need stitches.

13:06.785 --> 13:08.162
What? Really?

13:08.746 --> 13:09.955
A real machete?

13:10.039 --> 13:11.165
Yes.

13:11.832 --> 13:15.169
I wondered why I was woken up
in the middle of the night.

13:15.669 --> 13:18.172
I can't believe you were cut
by a kid with a machete.

13:19.173 --> 13:21.884
Teenagers these days are scary, huh?

13:21.967 --> 13:24.929
Normal teenagers don't wield machetes.

13:25.638 --> 13:28.974
Really? Every young boy
has a machete or two.

13:29.642 --> 13:30.643
Right?

13:31.143 --> 13:32.728
These barbarian siblings.

13:32.811 --> 13:35.898
You can have this back, Doctor.

13:35.981 --> 13:37.483
It's Asa-san's blood.

13:37.566 --> 13:39.151
Try not to walk around with that stuff.

13:39.235 --> 13:40.986
It's unsanitary.

13:42.029 --> 13:43.572
That's right! The blood!

13:43.656 --> 13:46.116
Only fiends draw blood
from living women and children.

13:46.700 --> 13:50.120
Actually, it was my idea
for him to take it.

13:50.871 --> 13:52.456
Modern technology allows us

13:52.540 --> 13:55.501
to draw only the needed amount
of blood without cutting veins.

13:56.752 --> 13:58.546
What? With magic?

13:58.629 --> 14:02.174
We had her blood drawn
here in this infirmary.

14:02.675 --> 14:04.718
You poke a person with this
and draw their blood out.

14:04.802 --> 14:07.721
It doesn't even hurt
when done by someone skilled.

14:07.805 --> 14:09.723
This is medicine? How does it work?

14:10.474 --> 14:14.603
He's fine with violence,
but drawing blood upsets him?

14:14.687 --> 14:16.814
I don't get his logic at all.

14:17.398 --> 14:20.568
Also, the Kagemori clan feeds me tons,

14:20.651 --> 14:22.778
so drawing a little blood doesn't hurt me.

14:26.949 --> 14:28.617
Can I hug you now?

14:28.701 --> 14:29.994
Absolutely not!

14:30.703 --> 14:32.621
Anyway, you're huge.

14:32.705 --> 14:35.666
Asa is smaller and cuter than that.

14:35.749 --> 14:39.503
You'll grow bigger, too,
if you eat the food they have down here.

14:40.170 --> 14:42.131
Isn't it salty, though?

14:42.882 --> 14:44.300
Is it?

14:44.383 --> 14:45.843
It's too strongly seasoned.

14:45.926 --> 14:49.013
I'm used to it.

14:49.096 --> 14:50.973
But the rice is good. Really good.

14:51.724 --> 14:54.393
Wait, I didn't come to talk about food.

14:54.476 --> 14:57.855
- You have questions for me, right?
- Yeah.

14:57.938 --> 14:59.940
Once we're done talking, can I hug you?

15:00.024 --> 15:02.693
You're determined, I'll give you that.

15:03.193 --> 15:06.614
They seem perfectly in tune
with each other.

15:10.409 --> 15:11.994
Where are Mother and Father?

15:14.079 --> 15:15.289
Let me see them.

15:15.372 --> 15:16.874
You fled the village together, didn't you?

15:20.628 --> 15:21.462
Yeah...

15:22.129 --> 15:24.131
- Then...
- They're not here.

15:25.049 --> 15:25.883
Then where?

15:27.259 --> 15:28.302
They're missing.

15:29.887 --> 15:32.431
I don't know where they are.

15:42.900 --> 15:45.444
- How much should I tell him?
- Everything.

15:46.570 --> 15:48.697
I don't want to lie to my brother.

15:56.705 --> 16:00.417
A lot happened
after your parents left the village.

16:00.918 --> 16:04.588
It was some time
after the Kagemoris took them in.

16:05.172 --> 16:06.799
They'd settled into their new lives,

16:06.882 --> 16:10.469
so they decided
to visit your mother's home.

16:11.303 --> 16:12.513
That's right.

16:12.596 --> 16:15.474
My mother said she was originally
from down the mountain.

16:15.975 --> 16:17.726
She said she wanted to take me there.

16:18.227 --> 16:20.854
Your mother is from Okinawa.

16:20.938 --> 16:23.983
Okinawa is an island far to the south.

16:24.650 --> 16:27.236
You have to take a plane
or boat to get there.

16:27.319 --> 16:29.363
A plane?

16:29.446 --> 16:31.865
We called them dragons in the village.

16:31.949 --> 16:34.159
Those are vehicles?

16:34.243 --> 16:37.246
Yeah. They can carry
about a hundred passengers.

16:37.830 --> 16:39.248
Down here, people thought Mother

16:39.331 --> 16:42.751
had gone missing
in some mountains in Tohoku,

16:43.419 --> 16:46.463
so she wanted to show her parents
back home that she was okay.

16:46.547 --> 16:52.261
They left me with the Kagemori clan,
and on the plane to Okinawa...

16:54.430 --> 16:55.264
our parents vanished.

16:58.267 --> 17:01.645
Did they fall from the dragon
from the plane?

17:01.729 --> 17:06.442
No, they somehow vanished
during their flight.

17:07.276 --> 17:09.820
They definitely boarded in Tokyo,

17:10.320 --> 17:13.782
but they weren't on the plane
when it arrived in Okinawa.

17:14.783 --> 17:16.368
Did someone kidnap them?

17:16.452 --> 17:17.703
We don't know.

17:17.786 --> 17:19.329
They didn't have anyone guarding them?

17:19.413 --> 17:20.789
They did.

17:21.707 --> 17:26.587
A reliable Kagemori Daemon Wielder
was assigned to guard them...

17:27.463 --> 17:29.298
but their guard disappeared with them.

17:30.716 --> 17:34.011
Then isn't that guard suspicious?

17:34.094 --> 17:36.096
Yeah, you're right.

17:36.638 --> 17:39.308
They could've been an enemy
pretending to be an ally.

17:40.059 --> 17:44.813
They could've been a Higashi Village agent
who infiltrated the Kagemori clan.

17:47.191 --> 17:50.402
Whatever their allegiance, I'm sorry.

17:50.486 --> 17:52.571
It was our mistake.

17:52.654 --> 17:56.909
You trust these guys
after they let our parents go missing?!

17:58.202 --> 17:59.703
After we left,

17:59.787 --> 18:03.624
assassins from the village came for us
one after another.

18:04.208 --> 18:06.251
It was ultimately the master

18:06.335 --> 18:09.505
of the Kagemori clan
and Jin-san's people who saved me.

18:12.925 --> 18:15.010
I trust the Kagemori clan.

18:30.859 --> 18:33.862
The boy entered the Kagemori manor.

18:33.946 --> 18:36.824
Jin did well.

18:36.907 --> 18:38.325
They're the first twins

18:38.408 --> 18:41.745
born in the eastern village in four
hundred years to sunder the night and day.

18:41.829 --> 18:45.833
Four hundred years! Four hundred years!
Four hundred years!

18:45.916 --> 18:49.002
Now both of them are down here.

18:49.086 --> 18:53.465
The jaw Daemon girl's mobility
is limited due to a leg injury.

18:53.549 --> 18:54.591
Jin is injured, too.

18:54.675 --> 18:56.426
And the master is away.

18:56.510 --> 18:58.428
This is a golden opportunity.

18:58.512 --> 19:01.098
We could seize both twins at once.

19:01.181 --> 19:02.683
Are you sure?

19:02.766 --> 19:06.478
The boy and his Daemons are quite capable.

19:06.562 --> 19:10.149
And the girl? The girl? The girl?

19:10.232 --> 19:11.441
It's nighttime.

19:11.525 --> 19:13.569
She's weaker now than during the day.

19:13.652 --> 19:15.028
As for the boy...

19:15.112 --> 19:17.322
Well, it's fine if he dies now.

19:17.406 --> 19:20.576
We only need the girl's head.

19:48.770 --> 19:52.524
What? It's still dark out.

19:57.779 --> 19:59.198
Oh?

19:59.781 --> 20:01.491
I don't recognize you.

20:10.500 --> 20:14.171
Jin, you lied! You led me into a trap!

20:14.254 --> 20:17.174
Actually, those aren't Kagemori Daemons.

20:17.841 --> 20:20.677
Outsiders have entered the manor.

20:21.261 --> 20:23.305
Can we defeat those Daemons?

20:23.931 --> 20:27.351
Ideally, I'd like to capture their master.

20:27.434 --> 20:28.894
Capture them?

20:29.478 --> 20:33.982
It'll be hard to find them
in this huge manor.

20:34.566 --> 20:38.320
If you're killing them,
make sure they're dead.

20:38.403 --> 20:40.739
I don't want to have to treat them.

20:40.822 --> 20:43.492
And you call yourself a doctor?!

20:44.076 --> 20:46.245
What happens to Daemons
when their master dies?

20:46.828 --> 20:48.956
If they're not transferred
to a new master before their death,

20:49.039 --> 20:50.499
they become stray Daemons.

20:50.582 --> 20:54.461
That's why Daemons usually
prioritize protecting their master.

20:58.757 --> 21:00.092
Stray Daemons?

21:00.801 --> 21:02.094
Their contract expires,

21:02.177 --> 21:04.179
and they're bound
to that location like ghosts.

21:05.013 --> 21:08.600
If they're forgotten
and a new contractor never appears,

21:08.684 --> 21:12.271
they vanish
after a few decades or centuries.

21:13.313 --> 21:15.107
That's rough.

21:15.190 --> 21:18.902
Got it. I'll try not to kill their master.

21:18.986 --> 21:20.529
You were going to kill them?!

21:20.612 --> 21:21.822
You're so nice!

21:22.614 --> 21:24.908
Jin, do they have a bow and arrows?

21:24.992 --> 21:25.826
Makoto-kun.

21:29.746 --> 21:30.998
What is this stuff?

21:31.081 --> 21:32.916
I've never used any of these before!

21:40.590 --> 21:43.885
I guess I'll try this one.

23:27.614 --> 23:28.907
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:28.990 --> 23:30.408
B-Brother!

23:30.992 --> 23:33.161
Then I'm free to do what I want, right?

23:34.079 --> 23:37.916
If my brother acquires
the power of Seal...

23:41.002 --> 23:41.920
Translator: Sho Stifler
